Lobium — a browser-process API to rescale a live device-metrics emulation session.

The Android device frame (branding/device-frame.patch) lays the real WebContents inside a centered
phone/tablet stage. It learns the exact scale that fits the aperture only from its own live views
layout — after startup, and again on every resize and whole-device zoom — which is far too late for
the renderer's emulation session, whose metrics were fixed when Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride
first ran. Nothing in content/ could adjust just the scale afterwards.

Re-sending the whole DeviceEmulationParams block from the browser process is not a substitute: it
races the DevTools session's own values, and SetDeviceEmulationParams clears the page cache whenever
any field differs, so a drag-resize would flush the cache once per layout frame.

So this adds the one narrow operation that was missing:

  EmulationHandler::SetDeviceEmulationScale(float)   — mutate DeviceEmulationParams::scale alone,
                                                       leaving screen size and device scale factor
                                                       untouched. False when no outermost main frame
                                                       is attached yet, which is the caller's signal
                                                       to retry on the next layout pass.
  content::SetLobiumDeviceEmulationScale(WebContents*, float)
                                                     — the //content public entry point the views
                                                       layer calls, fanning out to every emulation
                                                       handler attached to that WebContents.

Split out of device-frame.patch on purpose. That patch is chrome/browser/ui/views only; this one is
the //content API it consumes, and the two rebase against completely different upstream code. Build
wiring for both new files lives in core/build-gn.patch, which owns the GN graph.

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/lobium_device_emulation.cc b/content/browser/devtools/lobium_device_emulation.cc
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/lobium_device_emulation.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+// Copyright 2026 The Lobster Browser Authors.
+
+#include "content/public/browser/lobium_device_emulation.h"
+
+#include "content/browser/devtools/devtools_agent_host_impl.h"
+#include "content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/devtools_agent_host.h"
+
+namespace content {
+
+bool SetLobiumDeviceEmulationScale(WebContents* web_contents, float scale) {
+  if (!web_contents || scale <= 0.0f) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  scoped_refptr<DevToolsAgentHost> agent_host =
+      DevToolsAgentHost::GetOrCreateFor(web_contents);
+  if (!agent_host) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  bool updated = false;
+  auto* agent_host_impl =
+      static_cast<DevToolsAgentHostImpl*>(agent_host.get());
+  for (protocol::EmulationHandler* handler :
+       protocol::EmulationHandler::ForAgentHost(agent_host_impl)) {
+    updated = handler->SetDeviceEmulationScale(scale) || updated;
+  }
+  return updated;
+}
+
+}  // namespace content
diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc
--- a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc
@@ -1052,6 +1052,21 @@ blink::DeviceEmulationParams EmulationHandler::GetDeviceEmulationParams() {
   return device_emulation_params_;
 }
 
+bool EmulationHandler::SetDeviceEmulationScale(float scale) {
+  if (scale <= 0.f)
+    return false;
+  // Emulation state lives on the outermost main frame only; before one is
+  // attached there is no session to scale.
+  if (!host_ || host_->GetParentOrOuterDocument())
+    return false;
+  blink::DeviceEmulationParams params = GetDeviceEmulationParams();
+  if (params.scale == scale)
+    return true;
+  params.scale = scale;
+  SetDeviceEmulationParams(params);
+  return true;
+}
+
 void EmulationHandler::SetDeviceEmulationParams(
     const blink::DeviceEmulationParams& params) {
   DCHECK(host_);
diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h
--- a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h
@@ -130,6 +130,16 @@ class EmulationHandler : public DevToolsDomainHandler,
   blink::DeviceEmulationParams GetDeviceEmulationParams();
   void SetDeviceEmulationParams(const blink::DeviceEmulationParams& params);
 
+  // Lobium: update ONLY the compositor scale of an already-running device-metrics
+  // emulation session, leaving the emulated screen size and device scale factor
+  // alone. The device-frame view needs this because it learns the exact aperture
+  // fit only from live layout, long after Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride ran;
+  // re-sending the whole param block from the browser process would race the
+  // session's own values and clear the page cache on every resize frame.
+  // Returns false when there is nothing to scale (no outermost main frame yet),
+  // which is the caller's signal to retry on the next layout pass.
+  bool SetDeviceEmulationScale(float scale);
+
